From 25f8a43828204dd1226d5bf5c3b36547b4a07a40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:47:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: skip only the listed Teleport Other candidates when
 judging danger

The Teleport Other skip list holds borg_tp_other_n entries, but the
danger check walked ii <= borg_tp_other_n and also compared the entry
one past the count.  That slot keeps the index of a monster listed by an
earlier target candidate of the same evaluation, so after the list
became shorter the stale monster's danger was suppressed as if it were
about to be teleported away.  Stop at the last listed entry.

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-danger.c b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
index 11efe9f1a..8bf055bb5 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-danger.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
@@ -2321,7 +2321,7 @@ int borg_danger_one_kill(
      * checks in borg6.c in the defense maneuvers.
      */
     if (borg_tp_other_n) {
-        for (ii = 0; ii <= borg_tp_other_n; ii++) {
+        for (ii = 0; ii < borg_tp_other_n; ii++) {
             /* Is the current danger check same as a saved monster index? */
             if (i == borg_tp_other_index[ii]) {
                 return 0;
